  <p class="standfirst">Everyone wants to talk about where to post. Almost nobody asks what exactly is being posted.</p>

  <section class="tldr" aria-label="Summary">
    <h2>TL;DR</h2>
    <p>Brands are constantly told to publish more on LinkedIn, Reddit, Instagram, YouTube, and email. But distribution without a content foundation creates a treadmill: another post, another video, another idea, most of it gone within days.</p>
    <p>A better model starts with your owned property. Find a question your customer is asking, create the best answer you can, publish it on your website, then turn that answer into native formats for the channels where your customers actually spend time.</p>
    <p><strong>Distribution amplifies authority. It doesn't create it.</strong></p>
  </section>

